                  %a{:href => "#as_a_weighted_colimit"} As a weighted colimit
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} Ends
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coends"} coends
            are special sorts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
            and colimits –
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+ends"} homotopy ends
            and coends. Since a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivator"} derivator
            is a formal structure for computing homotopy limits and colimits, there are corresponding notions of ends and coends in a derivator.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivator"} derivator
            indexed on a 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Dia
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dia
            of diagram shapes, let
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Dia
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in Dia
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\in D(A^{op}\times A)
            %em coend
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            (obvious dualizations will yield its
            = succeed ")." do
              %em end
          %h3#as_a_colimit_over_simplices As a colimit over simplices
          %p
            One classical construction of a coend as a colimit proceeds by constructing an auxiliary category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi tw
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{tw}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (regarded as an object of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi tw
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{tw}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi tw
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon A^{tw}\to A^{op}\times A
            which sends each object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,x)
            and each arrow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon x\to y
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y,x)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\colon A^{op}\times A\to C
            can be constructed as the colimit of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi tw
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^* H\colon A^{tw}\to C
          %p
            We can mimic this in a derivator, except that we need to “homotopify”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi tw
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{tw}
            by including higher information as well. Thus, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta / A)^{op}
            denote the opposite of the category of simplices of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon [n]\to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon [n]\to A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\colon [m]\to A
            are functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [m]\to [n]
            making the evident triangle commute. There is a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon (\Delta / A)^{op} \to A^{op}\times A
            which sends
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon [n]\to A
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x(n), x(0))
          %p
            Note that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi tw
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{tw}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta / A)^{op}
            containing only the 0-simplices and 1-simplicies. The inclusion of this subcategory is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+functor"} final
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+final+functor"} homotopy final
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi tw
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{tw}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta / A)^{op}
          %p
            Hence, we define the
            %strong (homotopy) coend
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\in D(A^{op}\times A)
            to be the (homotopy) colimit of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi H
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^* H \in D((\Delta / A)^{op})
          %h3#as_a_colimit_over_arrows As a colimit over arrows
          %p
            Another classical construction of a coend as a colimit involves a different auxiliary category, the opposite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+arrow+category"} twisted arrow category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Tw
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tw(A)^{op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tw
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tw(A)^{op}
            are arrows
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon x\to y
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon x\to y
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi z
                  %mo →
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\colon z\to w
            are commutative squares
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi z
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi g
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                        %mtd
                          %mo ←
                        %mtd
                          %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  x &amp; \to &amp; z\\
                  ^f \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow^g\\
                  y &amp; \leftarrow &amp; w }
          %p
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Tw
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \colon Tw(A)^{op} \to A^{op}\times A
          %p
            sending
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon x\to y
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y,x)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\colon A^{op}\times A\to C
            can be constructed as the colimit of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Tw
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^* H\colon Tw(A)^{op} \to C
          %p
            Amazingly, this version needs no modification to become homotopical. Given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\in D(A^{op}\times A)
            in a derivator, we can simply restrict along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Tw
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tw(A)^{op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            via a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+final+functor"} homotopy final functor
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Tw
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi op
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi s
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mi r
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi A
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi op
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi q
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mi op
                          %mo ×
                          %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ &amp; &amp; Tw(A)^{op} \\
                  \&amp; ^{s}\nearrow &amp; &amp; \searrow^{r}\\
                  (\Delta / A)^{op} &amp; &amp; \underset{q}{\to} &amp; &amp; A^{op}\times A }
          %p
            The definition of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            is simple: we regard an
            = succeed "-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            composable arrows in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and take its composite. The morphisms in the two categories match nicely. To show that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            is homotopy final, we must show that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi A
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi op
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mi Tw
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi op
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{(\Delta / A)^{op} &amp; \xrightarrow{s} &amp; Tw(A)^{op} \\
                  \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \\
                  * &amp; \to &amp; * }
          %p
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+exact+square"} homotopy exact square
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+square"} comma square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Q
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi A
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi op
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mi Tw
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi op
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{Q_{f} &amp; \overset{}{\to} &amp; *\\
                  \\downarrow &amp; \swArrow &amp; \downarrow^{f}\\
                  (\Delta / A)^{op}&amp; \underset{}{\to} &amp; Tw(A)^{op}.}
          %p
            The objects of the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_{f}
            are strings of composable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\ge 2
            arrows whose composite is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta / A)^{op}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+bar+construction"} two-sided bar construction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(A(-,b),A,A(a,-))
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            However, the simplicial map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(A(-,b),A,A(a,-)) \to A(a,b)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(a,b)
            a discrete simplicial set, is well-known to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+equivalence"} simplicial homotopy equivalence
            and thus a weak equivalence of simplicial sets. Thus, each of its fibers is simplicially contractible, and hence each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_f
            has contractible nerve. This implies that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Q
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ Q_f &amp; \to &amp; * \\ \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \\ * &amp; \to &amp; * }
          %p
            is homotopy exact, and thus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            is homotopy final.
          %h3#as_a_bar_construction As a bar construction
          %p
            Another classical construction of a coend as a colimit is as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+pair"} parallel pair
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi x
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{f\colon x\to y} H(y,x) \;\rightrightarrows\; \coprod_{x} H(x,x).
          %p
            This can be obtained in a straightforward way from the previous construction. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ppr
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ppr
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+structure"} walking
            parallel pair
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1 \rightrightarrows 0)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi tw
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ppr
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q\colon A^{tw}\to Ppr
            sending each object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to 0, each arrow of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to 1, and sorting the morphisms by whether they map an arrow to its domain or to its codomain.
          %p
            Then the above parallel pair is the (pointwise)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi tw
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^* H \colon A^{tw} \to C
            along
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+opfibration"} discrete opfibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*H
            is equivalently its left Kan extension to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi tw
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \colim^{A^{tw}} p^* H
            is isomorphic to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                      %mi Ppr
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi q
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \colim^{Ppr} Lan_q p^* H
          %p
            We can homotopify this in a straightforward way as well. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon (\Delta / A)^{op} \to A^{op}\times A
            be as above, and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q\colon (\Delta / A)^{op} \to \Delta^{op}
            be the obvious forgetful functor (whose target is the opposite of the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ppr
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ppr
            is a final, but not homotopy-final, subcategory of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mi H
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^* H\in D((\Delta / A)^{op})
            can equivalently be calculated as the homotopy colimit of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mo !
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi H
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_! p^* H \in D(\Delta^{op})
          %p
            Note that since an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(\Delta^{op})
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            is also a discrete opfibration, and since pullbacks of fibrations are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+exact+square"} homotopy exact
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            are also computed as colimits over its fibers. These fibers are also discrete, so we obtain a simplicial diagram of the following sort:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                      %mo ←
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mo ←
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi x
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \coprod_{x_0\xrightarrow{f_1} x_1 \xrightarrow{f_2} x_2} H(x_2,x_0)
                  \\underoverset{\to}{\to}{\underoverset{\leftarrow}{\leftarrow}{\to}}
                  \\coprod_{x_0\xrightarrow{f_1} x_1} H(x_1,x_0)
                  \\underoverset{\to}{\to}{\leftarrow}
                  \\coprod_{x} H(x,x)
          %p
            This is a derivator version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+construction"} bar construction
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
          %h3#as_a_weighted_colimit As a weighted colimit
          %p
            A last classical construction of a coend is as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+colimit"} weighted colimit
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\colon A^{op}\times A\to C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom\colon A^{op}\times A \to Set
          %p
            In order to homotopify this, recall that weighted colimits can be constructed in terms of Kan extensions by first Kan extending to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collage"} collage
            of the weighting (pro)functor, then restricting to the target object. Thus, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            denote the collage of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom\colon A^{op}\times A \to Set
            regarded as a profunctor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mi ⇸
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 &amp;#8696; A^{op}\times A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\colon 1\to B
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\colon A^{op}\times A \to B
            %strong homotopy coend
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\in D(A^{op}\times A)
            to be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi u
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mo !
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u^* v_! H
          %p To show that this is the same as the previous definitions, we simply observe that there is a comma square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Tw
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi op
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi r
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mi op
                          %mo ×
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mo !
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mi α
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi v
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi u
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{Tw(A)^{op}&amp; \overset{r}{\to} &amp; A^{op}\times A\\
                  ^!\downarrow &amp; \swArrow_\alpha &amp; \downarrow^v\\
                  1&amp; \underset{u}{\to} &amp; B}
          %p
            Thus, by one of the axioms of a derivator,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi u
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mo !
                    %mi H
                    %mo ≅
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u^* v_! H \cong \colim (r^* H)
